  "strategy": "We are to create a step function sequence of non-negative coefficients that minimizes the evaluation metric:\n`2 * n * max(convolve(a, a)) / (sum(a))^2`\n\nWe'll use a combination of initialization, optimization, and search techniques:\n\n**Approach and rationale:**\n1. Initialization:\n   - Start by generating the \"height_sequence_1\" which is a sparse sequence with distinct peaks\n   - Also generate both padded and unpadded versions of promising structures\n\n2. Optimization pipeline:\n   A. Use gradient descent with momentum-based acceleration\n   B. Switch to LP-based refinement when gradient disappears\n   C. Final polish with coordinate descent\n   D. Exit criteria based on objective improvement pattern\n\n3. Search strategy:\n   - Try multiple lengths: 256, 384, 512\n   - Use multi-start optimization (three different initializations per length)\n   - Keep track of best solution found so far\n   - For each starting point, allow aggressive exploration phases\n\nThis approach uses:\n- Fewer but more aggressive optimization steps\n- Explicit construction of promising sequences (not relying on luck)\n- Adaptive learning rate reducing when high-frequency components stabilize\n- Early termination of suboptimal branches\n\nImplementation details:\n\n1. First generate the base \"height_sequence_1\" using known structure (concave then convex):\n   - Ar lines vary from low to high at different positions\n   - Base value smoothly decays from center to ends\n\n2. Then build auxiliary sequences by:\n   a. Center-aligned: (using the same base structure padded appropriately)\n   b. Mirrored/Flipped: to try different orientations\n   c. Linear interpolation: between high peaks\n\n3. Evaluate the potential sequences with decreasing learning rates until improvement plateaus\n\n4. Use the parent sequence's structure to guide the search:\n\nWe'll explicitly require the length to be 512 due to its balance of detail and computational feasibility.\n\nThe key is to combine structure-based initialization with flexible exploration.",
